<details>
<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (7)</summary><blockquote>

<details>
<summary>assets/css/invoice.css (7)</summary><blockquote>

`38-42`: **Duplicate and inconsistent heading rules (td vs th); consolidate to a single selector.**

Heading styles are spread across three blocks, mix `td` and `th`, and partially overlap. This invites maintenance drift and unpredictable overrides. Consolidate to a single rule that targets both `th` and `td`. Also set a darker text color to ensure adequate contrast over `#eee`.

Apply this consolidation:

```diff
-.invoice-box table tr.heading td {
-  background: #eee;
-  border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
-  font-weight: 500;
-}
-
-.invoice-box table tr.heading th {
-  border-left: 1px solid #ddd;
-  border-right: 1px solid #ddd;
-}
-
-.invoice-box table tr.heading th {
-  background: #eee;
-  border-top: 1px solid #ddd;
-  border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
-  padding: 10px;
-  text-align: right;
-  font-weight: bold;
-  text-transform: uppercase;
-  font-size: 80%;
-}
+/* Consolidated heading styles for both th and td */
+.invoice-box table tr.heading > th,
+.invoice-box table tr.heading > td {
+  background: #eee;
+  border-top: 1px solid #ddd;
+  border-right: 1px solid #ddd;
+  border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
+  border-left: 1px solid #ddd;
+  padding: 10px;
+  text-align: right;
+  font-weight: 700;
+  text-transform: uppercase;
+  font-size: 80%;
+  color: #333; /* better contrast on #eee */
+}
```


Also applies to: 48-51, 57-66

---

`20-22`: **Make numeric-column alignment resilient and RTL-friendly without hard-coding column index.**

Relying on `td:nth-child(2)` assumes the amount is always in column 2. If columns change, alignment breaks and requires the RTL override. Prefer aligning the last column and use logical alignment (`start`/`end`) to avoid separate RTL rules.


Apply this refactor and verify that the amounts indeed sit in the last column in the template:

```diff
-.invoice-box table tr td:nth-child(2) {
-  text-align: right;
-}
+/* Align totals/amounts in the last column */
+.invoice-box table tr > *:last-child {
+  text-align: end; /* resolves automatically for RTL */
+}
@@
-.rtl table tr td:nth-child(2) {
-  text-align: left;
-}
+/* No override needed when using logical alignment */
```

If some rows have action buttons or notes on the far right, consider adding a semantic class (e.g., `.col-amount`) on the amount cell and target that instead:
`.invoice-box .col-amount { text-align: end; }`


Also applies to: 113-115

---

`81-87`: **Totals row: avoid forcing all cells to right-align.**

Right-aligning every cell can hurt readability when labels should stay left/start-aligned. Right-align only the amount cell (e.g., `:last-child`) to keep labels readable.

Apply this tweak if labels appear misaligned:

```diff
-.invoice-box table tr.total td {
+.invoice-box table tr.total td:last-child {
   border-top: 2px solid #eee;
   font-weight: bold;
   padding-bottom: 60px;
   padding-top: 10px;
-  text-align: right;
+  text-align: end;
 }
```

---

`89-101`: **Responsive rules look good; consider also reducing huge title size on narrow screens.**

The stacking works nicely. On small screens the 45px title can overflow. Consider scaling it down under 600px.

Suggested addition:

```diff
 @media only screen and (max-width: 600px) {
   .invoice-box table tr.top table td {
     width: 100%;
     display: block;
     text-align: center;
   }
@@
   .invoice-box table tr.information table td {
     width: 100%;
     display: block;
     text-align: center;
   }
+  .invoice-box table tr.top table td.title {
+    font-size: 32px;
+    line-height: 36px;
+  }
 }
```

---

`103-111`: **RTL base is solid; prefer logical properties to reduce overrides.**

Since this layout is table-based, switching to logical text alignment (`start`/`end`) can remove the need for extra RTL overrides and reduce maintenance surface.

As in earlier comments, favor `text-align: start|end` and avoid left/right-specific rules where possible. No action required if you need to support very old browsers.

---

`1-7`: **Optional: set a practical max-width for nicer on-screen reading.**

`width: 100%` is fine for PDF/print, but a `max-width` (e.g., 800px) improves readability in the browser preview while still printing full-width as needed.

Example:

```diff
 .invoice-box {
-  width: 100%;
+  width: 100%;
+  max-width: 800px;
   margin: auto;
   font-size: 16px;
   line-height: 24px;
   color: #555;
 }
```

---

`115-115`: **Add minimal print rules to improve PDF/print fidelity.**

Backgrounds are often dropped by printers unless explicitly allowed. These hints improve consistency across HTML-to-PDF engines and native print.

Apply at end of file:

```diff
+@media print {
+  /* Try to preserve backgrounds and colors in print/PDF where supported */
+  * {
+    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
+    print-color-adjust: exact;
+  }
+  /* Avoid row splits where possible */
+  .invoice-box table tr {
+    break-inside: avoid;
+    page-break-inside: avoid;
+  }
+}
```

